module org.kde.plasma.workspace.osd
# AedwenOS shadow of Plasma's OSD module. plasmashell loads the on-screen
# display (volume, brightness, mute, power profile...) by module name, and
# Plasma 6.8 has no other way to restyle it: the stock QML is compiled into
# plasmashell_osd.so ("prefer :/qt/qml/..."), so files on disk are ignored.
# /etc/xdg/plasma-workspace/env/aedwen-qml.sh puts /usr/share/aedwen/qml
# ahead of the system import path, so this module wins. It needs none of
# Plasma's C++ (OsdWindow): plasmashell only sets plain properties on the
# root object -- see Osd.qml. OsdItem is exported too: the lock screens
# (ours and Plasma's LockOsd.qml) import it from this module.
Osd 254.0 Osd.qml
OsdItem 254.0 OsdItem.qml
